# 🪟 Windows Administration

## Local Users & Groups

Local Users & Groups is a Windows management tool used to:

* Create local users
* Modify users
* Delete users
* Create local groups
* Manage local group membership

---

## Local User

A Local User account exists only on one computer.

Example:

Home computer.

Characteristics:

* Managed locally
* Cannot log into other computers

---

## Domain User

A Domain User account is created in Active Directory.

Characteristics:

* Centrally managed
* Can log into multiple domain-joined computers (based on permissions)
* Managed by the Domain Controller

---

## Administrator vs Standard User

### Administrator

Can:

* Install software
* Change system settings
* Manage users
* Install drivers
* Run administrative tools

---

### Standard User

Can:

* Use applications
* Access permitted files
* Cannot perform administrative changes without approval

